WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Your cells never touch
your blood directly.

2
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:06.580
Instead, every cell is
bathed in tissue fluid,

3
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.790
and swaps substances with that.

4
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.090
That fluid comes from your blood.

5
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.760
Blood pressure squeezes it out
through the thin capillary walls.

6
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.880
It happens all day long, in every tissue.

7
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.510
So why don't your tissues flood?

8
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.520
In this mission, you'll
compare three body fluids,

9
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.620
and see what blood keeps back.

10
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.220
Then you'll follow that
fluid's whole journey,

11
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.550
from the blood, around
the cells, and onwards.

12
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.960
Your mission: explain why
your tissues don't flood,

13
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.640
though your blood vessels
leak fluid all day long.
